# Implementation phases (default)

**Do not mix phases.** Finish the current phase exit gate before starting the next. Track status in `CURSOR.md` Project Profile → **Current phase**.

| Phase | Name | Focus |
|-------|------|--------|
| **P0** | Foundation | Concept lock, tokens, folder skeleton, PHP migrations (+ seeds if needed) |
| **P1** | Mock UI + mock data | All surfaces on mocks — no real API required |
| **P2** | API backend | Real API on applied schema — UI may still use mocks |
| **P3** | Integration | Wire UI → API; remove/replace mock data usage |
| **P4** | Cleanup & ship | Dead code, docs, final testing |

Customize sub-bullets from **concept** during install; keep phase order.

---

## Phase exit gate (every phase)

At the **end** of each phase, run this gate **before** opening the next phase. Write leftovers into Profile / `concept-domain.mdc` / a short `PHASE_NOTES` section in `CURSOR.md`.

### Exit checklist (copy per phase)

- [ ] All **sub-tasks** for this phase done or explicitly deferred
- [ ] **Defaults** still intact (forms, ui-styling, validation, PHP migrate/seed, icons-states)
- [ ] Smoke / manual **test** of this phase’s deliverables passed
- [ ] Known bugs listed (fix now vs carry to next phase)
- [ ] Gaps / adds for **next phase** written down (not chat-only)
- [ ] Nothing from a **later** phase was half-started (or reverted / parked)
- [ ] User/AI agree: **exit OK** → advance Current phase

If anything fails: fix or document carry-over — do **not** silently advance.

---

## P0 — Foundation

### Subs

- [ ] P0.1 Intake complete — Profile + `concept-domain.mdc` filled
- [ ] P0.2 Scope lock — v1 in/out of scope
- [ ] P0.3 Design tokens + `frontend-design` skill filled
- [ ] P0.4 Repo skeleton (web/api/migrations/seeds per stack)
- [ ] P0.5 PHP migrations for concept entities (`up`/`down`) — **no `.sql`**
- [ ] P0.6 Seed.php / seeds for baseline demo data (if needed)
- [ ] P0.7 `.env.example` documented; app boots empty/skeleton
- [ ] P0.8 Unified form primitives scaffold planned or stubbed
- [ ] P0.9 Icon system recorded (`material` \| `lottie`); shared 404/error/empty + skeleton + lazy-load plan noted

### Exit (P0 → P1)

Run **Phase exit gate**. Especially verify: schema matches concept; no feature UI pretending to be done; carry list for P1 screens.

---

## P1 — Mock UI + mock data

### Subs

- [ ] P1.1 Routing shells per role/surface from concept
- [ ] P1.2 Marketing / baseline UI (if in scope)
- [ ] P1.3 All v1 screens on **mock data** (happy paths)
- [ ] P1.4 Unified **custom forms** on all inputs (defaults)
- [ ] P1.5 Client validation UX wired to shared form errors
- [ ] P1.6 Shared **404**, status-error, and **empty data** screens (animated per `icons-states.mdc`)
- [ ] P1.7 **Skeleton loaders** on async list/detail regions
- [ ] P1.8 **Lazy-loaded** routes/chunks wired
- [ ] P1.9 Responsive check on agreed breakpoints
- [ ] P1.10 SEO stubs only if Profile SEO = `on` (full Schema.org can wait for P3/P4 if noted)

### Exit (P1 → P2)

Run **Phase exit gate**. Especially verify: no accidental real API coupling; mock modules listed for P3 removal; missing screens deferred with reason; 404/empty/skeleton/lazy present.

---

## P2 — API backend

### Subs

- [ ] P2.1 Migrations applied on local/empty DB
- [ ] P2.2 Auth + role middleware
- [ ] P2.3 CRUD/query endpoints for concept entities
- [ ] P2.4 **Server validation** on all writes (default)
- [ ] P2.5 Consistent JSON success/error shapes
- [ ] P2.6 Upload/payment/etc. endpoints if in concept
- [ ] P2.7 Seeds usable for API smoke tests
- [ ] P2.8 API smoke tests / manual Postman-style checks

### Exit (P2 → P3)

Run **Phase exit gate**. Especially verify: UI still on mocks is OK; contract list (routes + payloads) ready for P3; authz covered.

---

## P3 — Integration (API ↔ UI) + mock cleanup

### Subs

- [ ] P3.1 API client / services replace mock adapters per feature
- [ ] P3.2 Auth session/token wiring in UI
- [ ] P3.3 Map API errors → form field errors
- [ ] P3.4 Feature-by-feature cutover (do not big-bang if risky)
- [ ] P3.5 **Remove or quarantine mock data** used in production paths
- [ ] P3.6 Keep mocks only behind explicit dev flag (or delete)
- [ ] P3.7 SEO meta + Schema.org if SEO = `on`
- [ ] P3.8 End-to-end happy paths on real API

### Exit (P3 → P4)

Run **Phase exit gate**. Especially verify: no silent mock fallbacks in prod builds; leftover mocks listed for P4 delete; integration bugs triaged.

---

## P4 — Cleanup, documentation, final testing

### Subs

- [ ] P4.1 Delete dead code, unused routes, leftover mocks
- [ ] P4.2 Docs: README / setup / env / migrate+seed commands
- [ ] P4.3 Final regression pass (roles × critical flows)
- [ ] P4.4 a11y spot-check on forms; security smoke (authz, uploads)
- [ ] P4.5 Performance sanity (main pages)
- [ ] P4.6 Deploy checklist from `/deploy` if shipping
- [ ] P4.7 Phase notes closed; Profile Current phase = `done` / `P4 complete`

### Exit (P4 → done)

Run **Phase exit gate**. No open P0–P3 carry items unless accepted as known backlog. Ship only when exit OK.

---

## AI behavior

1. Read **Current phase** before coding.
2. Only implement sub-tasks for that phase (unless fixing a blocking bug).
3. At phase end: run exit gate with the user; update carry-over list; then bump Current phase.
4. Prefer `/phase-exit` command when finishing a phase.
